---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

export const title = "Summiting Mt. Baker with SheJumps";
export const date = "2024-07-13";
export const excerpt = "My first mountaineering experience: six months of training, a fundraiser at a wine bar, and an alpine start at 4am with eight other women on a glaciated volcano.";
export const tags = ["mountaineering", "shejumps", "washington", "glacier"];
---

<SiteLayout title={`${title} — Saachi K Gupta`}>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <p style="opacity:0.7; font-size: 13px;">{date}</p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    I've never considered myself athletic. I grew up doing things like hiking, swimming, and riding bikes, but was never much of a gym-class or team sports person. I'd dabbled in a few 5K and 10K road races, but signing up to climb Baker with SheJumps as a Fundraiser was a big step for me. 
  </p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    Declaring a lofty intention publicly, working toward it, and then pushing through on the actual day was daunting, but lessened my fear of being public with my goals.
  </p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">Six months of training</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The SheJumps climb required being comfortable and capable carrying 35+ lbs at a pace of 1K gain over a mile in under an hour. I read about gym programs to get there, but the prospect of so much stairmaster was not appealing to me. Instead, I spent a lot of time hiking with a heavy pack, snowshoeing, outdoor stair repeats in Seattle, backpacking trips, and triathlon cross-training (swimming and cycling alongside the running). Essentially, my prep was snacpacking with my friends, and being luxurious with pack weight. 
  </p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    I'd already done a women's NOLS mountaineering course in Alaska in 2023 and had my Wilderness First Aid certification through SheJumps. Baker felt like it was attainable, but a stretch.
  </p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">The fundraiser</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    Each climber had to raise $2,400 for SheJumps on top of a $500 registration deposit. I organized a fundraising party at MoRa, a natural wine bar in Seattle, with help from friends who donated space, DJ'd, and put together a raffle with artwork and experiences. The evening raised over $1K for SheJumps and introduced a lot of people to each other. I ended up raising $2,776 personally, with some of it matched by corporate donations. The nine of us collectively raised over $20K.
  </p>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    SheJumps runs 200+ events a year, more than half of which are free or donation-based. I'd been a beneficiary myself, of a Wilderness First Aid course for BIPOC women that gave me a community I still lean on, and this felt like the right way to pay it forward.
  </p>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">The climb</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    We started the approach on July 12th at Park Butte Trailhead, camping at Sandy Camp. At 4am on July 13th, we put on crampons and headlamps and started moving.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/predawn.jpg"
      alt="Mt. Baker silhouette against a deep blue pre-dawn sky, two stars visible"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>4am. The mountain before the sun.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/glacier-climb.jpg"
      alt="Climbers roped together on the glacier at sunrise, Cascades visible below"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>Roped up on the glacier. The AAI guides taught us glacier travel, ice axe technique, and crevasse awareness.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/glacier-view.jpg"
      alt="Looking down the glacier from high on Baker — snow field, exposed rock, blue sky"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
  </figure>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch; margin-top: 16px;">
    The summit was clear with views of the San Juans. It was awe inspiring to have been at Sucia Island in the San Juans a few weeks prior, and now glimpsing the island from the summit of Baker. 
  </p>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/summit-saachi.jpg"
      alt="Saachi at the summit, smiling, blue helmet, red pack, pure blue sky behind"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>Summit, July 13, 2024.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/summit-group.jpg"
      alt="Nine women on the summit holding a SheJumps flag"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>The Group!</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">After</h2>

  <figure>
    <img
      src="/images/baker/high-camp.jpg"
      alt="Two people resting at high camp — tent, rocks, Cascades panorama spread out behind"
      style="border-radius: 8px;"
    />
    <figcaption>High camp. Exhausted. Worth it.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The experience of declaring a goal, training for it in my own way, and finishing it surrounded by other women was extremely energizing. I loved getting to do something new and difficult with a community of supportive women, and left the climb with new friends.
  </p>

</SiteLayout>
